			<<He>> goes very still.
			<br><br>

			For a long moment <<he>> says nothing at all. <<His>> fingers tap once against the rim of <<his>> glass, then stop.
			<br><br>

			"...A sudden invitation. Yes. I imagine it would be." <<He>> leans back, choosing <<his>> next words with care. "I have heard things about that bank. Whispers from the wrong rooms. The branch is real enough, the charity even more so, but <span class="elk">the owner</span> is a name that surfaces in places it shouldn't."
			<br><br>

			<<He>> watches you from behind the mask. "If Avery is being courted by them, then there will be something at that gala that isn't meant for the guest list. Look around, when you can. I trust your eye for detail, and I'd rather hear it from you than chase rumours."

